What Kobo found:
  active aliases at @strict block entry
Why this matters:
  value has 1 active alias when the @strict block starts; all aliases must end before the boundary
  is entered
Try this:
  drop or explicitly clone-then-drop aliases before the @strict { } boundary
More:
  Run `kobo explain K0041` for examples and deeper context.
error[K0042]: closure captures value across @strict boundary
  --> tests\ui\strict_k0042_closure_capture.kobo:5:27
  |
5 |         let f = || data.borrow_mut().push(4);
  |         ------------------------------------- @strict block here
5 |         let f = || data.borrow_mut().push(4);
  |                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ closure captures a shared mutable binding across @strict boundary
  |
What Kobo found:
  closure captures a shared mutable binding across @strict boundary
Why this matters:
  a closure defined inside an @strict block captures a shared mutable binding; calling the closure
  later could keep the strict borrow alive after the block ends
Try this:
  extract the closure outside the @strict block, or refactor to avoid capturing the guarded value
More:
  Run `kobo explain K0042` for examples and deeper context.
